    <!-- ==================== QWeather ==================== -->
    <string name="qweather_title">QWeather fallback</string>
    <string name="qweather_intro">QWeather (和风天气) is a Chinese weather service hosted in mainland China, no VPN needed, used as the last fallback.\n\nHow to get credentials:\n1. Open console.qweather.com, register and complete verification\n2. Project Management → create a project\n3. In the project: + Add credential → choose API KEY\n4. Go to Settings and copy your API Host (looks like xxxx.qweatherapi.com)\n5. Fill Host and Key below, then tap Test connection\n\nThe free plan allows 1000 calls a day; this app asks at most once every 30 minutes per city.</string>
    <string name="qweather_builtin_note">This build already has fallback credentials baked in, so you can leave these empty. The fields below only override them (empty = use the built-in).</string>
